 "title": "Verticillium dahliae Pathogenicity and Protein Secretion",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the pathogenic fungus Verticillium dahliae and its interactions with various organisms and chemicals. V. dahliae has pathogenicity towards Cotton and expresses several proteins, including AAs, CAZymes, CBMs, G2WZT4, and SCRPs. The fungus is also associated with the ΔVdMFS2 mutants and Vd592, which has a growth medium of Czapek-Dox medium and secretes more proteins than Vd592Y. The VdMFS2 gene is expressed in Cotton and silenced by HIGS, while V. dahliae is silenced by VdMFS2. The cluster also includes various methods and tools, such as pTRV2-00, pTRV2 vector, and Student’s t-test, which are used to study the fungus and its interactions.",
